-- Sale of Goods Act 1979 (Singapore), 2020 RE, informal consolidation in force from 1/4/2022.
-- LAYER 1: ROUTES TO ONE LEGAL EFFECT, GATHERED BY HAND (E1 option B).
-- The Act states the right to reject the goods, and the claim in damages, in several sections.
-- Each section's own answer is its own function in its Part module (option C).  The functions below gather those answers
-- by hand for the two effects a buyer asks about; they add no rule of their own, and they say so in the fork register.
-- Ruling E1 (2026-11-04): the Act has no construct that gathers an effect by name; this is a hand-gather, not a language feature.
-- JUST TRUE / JUST FALSE are answers the text gives in its own words; NOTHING is "the Act does not answer on
-- these facts".  A caller must never turn NOTHING into FALSE.

IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `soga-nouns`

§ `Routes gathered by hand`

-- The right to reject the goods: the routes in ss 12(1), 13(1), 14(2), 14(3), 15(2) and 30, and what stops them in ss 11(3), 15A(1) and 53(1).
-- src:353 | (3) Subject to section 35A, where a contract of sale is not severable
-- src:354 | and the buyer has accepted the goods or part of them, the breach of a
-- src:355 | condition to be fulfilled by the seller can only be treated as a breach of
-- src:356 | warranty, and not as a ground for rejecting the goods and treating the
-- src:357 | contract as repudiated, unless there is an express or implied term of
-- src:358 | the contract to that effect.
-- src:544 | 15A.—(1) Where in the case of a contract of sale —
-- src:546 | (a) the buyer would, apart from this subsection, have the right
-- src:547 | to reject goods by reason of a breach on the part of the
-- src:548 | seller of a condition implied by section 13, 14 or 15; but
-- src:550 | (b) the breach is so slight that it would be unreasonable for the
-- src:551 | buyer to reject them,
-- src:553 | then, if the buyer does not deal as consumer, the breach is not to be
-- src:554 | treated as a breach of condition but may be treated as a breach of
-- src:555 | warranty.
-- src:557 | (2) This section applies unless a contrary intention appears in, or is
-- src:558 | to be implied from, the contract.
-- src:1410 | 53.—(1) Where there is a breach of warranty by the seller, or where
-- src:1411 | the buyer elects (or is compelled) to treat any breach of a condition on
-- src:1412 | the part of the seller as a breach of warranty, the buyer is not by reason
-- src:1413 | only of such breach of warranty entitled to reject the goods; but he
-- src:1414 | may —
@ref route reject (src:353-358) (src:544-558) (src:1410-1414)
GIVEN `s 12(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 13(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 14(2) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 14(3) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 15(2)(a) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 15(2)(b) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 30(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 30(2) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 11(3) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 15A(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 53(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `route (E1 B) the buyer has the right to reject the goods` IS
    BRANCH
        IF   (`s 12(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 13(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 14(2) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 14(3) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 15(2)(a) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 15(2)(b) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 30(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 30(2) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE)
         AND (`s 11(3) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 15A(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 53(1) answer` EQUALS JUST FALSE)
        THEN
            -- FALSE-kind (the text says no in its own words): "can only be treated as a breach of warranty, and not as a ground for rejecting the goods" (s 11(3)); "the breach is not to be treated as a breach of condition but may be treated as a breach of warranty" (s 15A(1)); "the buyer is not by reason only of such breach of warranty entitled to reject the goods" (s 53(1)).
            JUST FALSE
        IF `s 12(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 13(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 14(2) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 14(3) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 15(2)(a) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 15(2)(b) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 30(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 30(2) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): none of the eight listed routes applies on these answers; other routes (an express term, time of the essence under s 10, s 11(2)) are not among the inputs.
            NOTHING

-- The buyer's claim in damages against the seller: ss 51(1) and 53(1)(b).
-- src:1375 | 51.—(1) Where the seller wrongfully neglects or refuses to deliver
-- src:1376 | the goods to the buyer, the buyer may maintain an action against the
-- src:1377 | seller for damages for non-delivery.
-- src:1410 | 53.—(1) Where there is a breach of warranty by the seller, or where
-- src:1411 | the buyer elects (or is compelled) to treat any breach of a condition on
-- src:1412 | the part of the seller as a breach of warranty, the buyer is not by reason
-- src:1413 | only of such breach of warranty entitled to reject the goods; but he
-- src:1414 | may —
-- src:1422 | (b) maintain an action against the seller for damages for the
-- src:1423 | breach of warranty.
@ref route damages (src:1375-1377) (src:1410-1414) (src:1422-1423)
GIVEN `s 51(1) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
      `s 53(1)(b) answer` IS A MAYBE BOOLEAN
GIVETH A MAYBE BOOLEAN
DECIDE `route (E1 B) the buyer may maintain an action against the seller for damages` IS
    BRANCH
        IF `s 51(1) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE OR `s 53(1)(b) answer` EQUALS JUST TRUE
        THEN JUST TRUE
        OTHERWISE
            -- NOTHING-kind (list not closed): neither s 51(1) nor s 53(1)(b) applies on these answers; the Act does not say the buyer has no other action for damages.
            NOTHING
